    "narrative": "The Austin Waves hold a distinct advantage today against favorable matchups, with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** leading the charge at a 72.87 efficiency score. Despite a moderate challenge from Bassitt, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a significant park factor boost, making him our highest-projected asset for run production. Close behind is **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 70.59 score remains strong despite a platoon disadvantage against Corbin; his ability to exploit the soft matchup against a 4.42 xERA pitcher\u2014combined with the expected #2 slot\u2014keeps him in must-start territory. **Sam Antonacci** rounds out our top trio (67.67) by leveraging a prime lead-off spot against Woods Richardson, whose 4.89 xERA offers the cleanest path to scoring for our roster today.\n\nOur most difficult personnel decision centered on **Miguel Vargas**, who posted a 60.61 score but ultimately landed on the bench behind **Josh Jung** and **Coby Mayo**. While **Miguel Vargas** earns points for his efficiency against Woods Richardson, the raw projection and situational leverage of **Josh Jung** in the heart of the order edged him out. We are closely monitoring the status of **Coby Mayo** and **Gunnar Henderson**, as the \"Lineup Pending\" designation introduces minor volatility. **Dominic Smith** was never a serious consideration for the starting nine; his sub-40 score is compounded by a 35% rain risk and a poor platoon matchup against Tolle, signaling a clear \"do not start\" to preserve our precious game caps. With **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Kyle Tucker** unavailable, we are banking on the current configuration to maximize our 5x5 output through volume and favorable SP matchups.",
